>
	<p>
		The Trend Times is an independent publication about AI tooling, agent infrastructure, and the
		economics of software. We read primary documents and report what they measure, who measured it,
		and where the evidence stops.
	</p>

	<h2>Who publishes this</h2>
	<p>
		The Trend Times is edited and published by <strong>Jaewon Oh</strong>, an independent developer
		based in South Korea. He sets the editorial direction, reviews every briefing before it is
		published, and answers corrections.
	</p>
	<p>
		There is no newsroom behind that name. The site is written by its editor with software tools, and
		the editor is accountable for everything published here. We do not publish sponsored articles and
		we do not accept payment for coverage.
	</p>

	<h2>How a briefing is made</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>
			<strong>Primary sources first.</strong> Every briefing starts from primary material: papers and
			preprints, vendor documentation and engineering posts, published surveys, and official reports.
			We cite the document itself, not a summary of it.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Every number is tied to a source.</strong> Figures, version numbers, and dates are checked
			against the original text before drafting. When a source is paywalled or was cached, we say what
			we could not read instead of filling the gap.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Automated checks before publishing.</strong> A verification script tests every outbound
			link, checks headline and description length, and confirms that each figure in a draft is bound
			to a listed source. A draft that fails is revised or dropped.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Review by the editor.</strong> The editor reviews each article for accuracy, attribution,
			and readability before it goes live. AI assistants help with research and drafting. The editor
			decides what publishes and is responsible for the result.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Corrections.</strong> When we get something wrong, we fix it and note the change and the
			date on the article.
		</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>What we are not</h2>
	<p>
		We are not a news wire and we do not give investment, legal, or tax advice. Read our
		<a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> and <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> for the full detail.
	</p>

	<h2>Advertising</h2>
	<p>
		The site does not carry advertising today. If we start to, the ads will be served by third parties
		such as Google AdSense, marked as ads, and kept away from editorial decisions. An advertiser cannot
		buy a mention, see an article before publication, or have one changed after it.
	</p>

